# Anti-Slop Policy

## Purpose

Agents must not ship plausible-but-wrong code. Slop = code that compiles, looks idiomatic, and fails CI or operator trust.

Remediation gates: `ci.mdc` (static gates), `ui.mdc` (admin anti-slop). Verification honesty: `quality.mdc`.

## Lie modes (never)

| Lie mode | Project-specific example |
| :--- | :--- |
| Wrong naming | Cryptic suffixes (`m8`, `n1`, `f1`) or legacy tokens (`BidShard`, `espx`) per `naming.mdc` |
| Charset slop | Emojis, Unicode dashes, ellipsis char, `===`/`---` banners in comments and `scripts/` echo/log (`comments.mdc`) |
| Wrong types | sqlc row field vs admin `FooDTO` `json` tag mismatch on `/api/v1` handlers |
| Plausible wrong logic | Parser budget bypass, budget invariant drift, outbox double-apply |
| Weakened tests | Green CI by removing `AssertBudgetInvariant` or chaos assertions |
| Unrun claims | Claiming `make test-alloc-gate` or `pr_fast.sh` passed without executing |
| Compile/test ritual | `go build ./...`, `go test -c ./...`, repeated package builds, or `npm run typecheck` without operator ask; burns RAM/CPU on shared dev machines |
| Tautological test | `require.Equal(t, x, x)` or table that only mirrors mock setup; survives revert of fix |
| Mutation survivor | Tests stay green if production `if` inverted; no `*_holdout` negative |
| Black-box fiction | "Hidden CI will catch it" without naming `test-integration` / `test-fault` tier |
| Mock bench as SLA | Citing `BenchmarkUnifiedFilter_Check_mock` ns/op as production `/track` p99 |
| Invented artifacts | Fake BPF reports, env vars, or benchmark output under `var/load-test/` |
| Doc ahead of code | Admin flag or doc behavior with no hot-path reader; cite `deploy/vendor/ANTIFRAUD.md` |
| Partial rename as shipped | Migration/UI/API field renamed (`silent_reject_enabled`) while ingestion, outbox, or reports still use old semantics |
| ML action semantics lie | Doc or operator text implies per-IP ghosting; code flips campaign PG flag or only enqueues when flag already on |
| Analytics name drift | Reports/UI still `ghost_*` while wire/CH uses `silent_reject_event`; funnels under-count silent rejects |
| Product-prefixed embed paths | Static like `ad-event-processor-track.js` / `adEventProcessorTrack` in shipped snippets (canonical: neutral `track.js`, export `trackEvent` when `web/src/static/` returns) |
| Marketing in tech docs | `naming.mdc` Forbidden marketing prose; doc lie rows below |
| Gate bureaucracy | New `*_gate.sh` that only wraps existing gates, or `exit 0` when the named check failed |
| Orchestrator double-run | `pr_fast.sh` child re-invokes a gate `pr_fast` already runs (naming, `admin_web`, skip-reason scan) |
| Admin doc ask -> code | Operator requests `.mdc` update; agent patches code | Spec-only until operator requests implementation (`ui.mdc`) |
| Admin piecemeal tree | Partial `web/` delete/refactor leaving broken imports | Atomic `web/` recreate per operator direction; server stub stays in `internal/controlplane/admin_static_stub/` |
| Admin phantom contract | "See prior contract" with no table in repo | Width/grid/error contracts live in `ui.mdc` |
| Admin unrun UI gates | Claims `typecheck` / `admin/web.sh` without output | Paste command + exit code (`quality.mdc`) |

## LLM dishonesty patterns

Recurring ways agents ship plausible diffs that fail review. Generalized from admin rebuild and cold-path work; not a session log. Cross-ref: `ui.mdc`, `boundaries.mdc`.

### Lie types

| Lie type | What the agent implies | What is actually true | Required behavior |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Doc ask -> code | Spec or rule update is done | Code or CSS changed on a doc-only turn | Zero implementation diff until explicit implement ask |
| Symptom patch | Visual bug fixed | Root layout contract unchanged; bug returns | Write invariant in `ui.mdc` first; code only when asked to implement |
| Phantom contract | "See prior contract" / "as before" | Pointer target missing or deleted | Full table in `ui.mdc` |
| Stale cross-doc | One rule file updated | Other index consumers still contradict | Same pass updates all linked rules (`development.mdc`, `core.mdc`, etc.) |
| Unrun verification | typecheck / gate / test passed | Command not executed or no output pasted | Paste command + path + exit code; or state not run (`quality.mdc`) |
| Piecemeal tree change | Incremental progress | Half-deleted tree, broken imports, mixed eras | Atomic remove or recreate per operator direction; server stub stays embed-only |
| Scope creep | "Small related fix" | Handlers, embed, Docker, CI touched without ask | List server-touching steps in the PR before doing them |
| Git archaeology | Restored "working" UI from old commit | Pre-spec patterns return (wrappers, stale layout, custom overlays) | Rebuild from `ui.mdc` + OpenAPI; no history copy without waiver |
| Wrapper stack | New chrome fixes layout | Matryoshka abstractions hide section grid contract | One section = one module; revert on reject, no compensating wrappers |
| Layout contract drift | Page "works" in preview | Macro shell built from flex columns; hand-rolled overlays | Macro Grid + micro Flex per `ui.mdc`; headless primitives for overlays |
| Double chrome | Chip/badge looks correct | Nested borders/padding on parent + child | One chip root; parent renders chip directly |
| Client cold-path smuggle | Fast interactive filters | `useMemo` sort/filter or business rules in browser | Server query params; client fetch + parse only |
| Layer on rejection | "One more fix" after stop | Rejected architecture compounds | `git revert` slice; deliver only what was asked |
| Abstract backlog | "Implement customers page" | No route/API/content | OpenAPI + handler contract first; rejected until filled |
| Backlog as mini-spec | OpenAPI/React prose duplicated in vendor docs | Rules live in `.mdc` | Link `ui.mdc` / OpenAPI; implementation detail in PR only |
| Static boot drift | Stub HTML "helpful" placeholder | Non-empty `#root` breaks boot inject / route tests | Empty `<div id="root"></div>` in stub; holdout in static route tests |

### Laziness shortcuts

| Shortcut | Agent motive | Cost | Instead |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Smallest visible diff | Close task quickly | Wrong architecture ships | Read intent; rules before files |
| Green at any cost | Merge narrative | CI or tests lie | Run named gate or say not run |
| Context amnesia | Rewrite rules from memory | Lost contracts | Diff rules against git; merge, do not replace blind |
| History copy | Blank spec | Rejected patterns return | Paths from current tree + `ui.mdc` only |
| Plausible fiction | "Should pass", "wired", "prior contract" | Operator audit fails | Falsify every claim with pasted command + exit code |
| Scope escape on doc task | "While I'm here" | Doc turn ships code + CI | Doc-only turn = docs only |
| Matryoshka structure | New folder/gate/wrapper | Bureaucracy slop | Extend leaf gate or single orchestrator |
| Tautology / example-only test | One happy table row | Mutation survives revert | `*_holdout` negative or corpus/fuzz row |

### On operator rejection

Stop implementation. Do not add wrappers, portals, or CI layers. Revert the rejected slice if already landed. Deliver only what was asked (rules, backlog, or atomic delete).

## Admin UI status

`web/` active — React 19 + TSX + Tailwind + shadcn/ui. Boot stub until `web/dist` embeds: `internal/controlplane/admin_static_stub/`. Contract: `ui.mdc` + `frontend-modular.mdc` + OpenAPI. Spec-only or doc-only ask: no code diff in the same turn. Rejected slice: revert; no compensating wrappers or portals.

## Hot path dishonesty (ingestion, broker, stream, tests)

`/track` and ingest wiring are where agents most often claim **"wired"** while tests only exercise **mocks, void sinks, or skipped integration**. Canonical boundary catalog: `boundaries.mdc` (**Test dishonesty catalog**). Cross-ref: `hot-path.mdc`, `tradeoffs.mdc`, `fault-tests.mdc`, `testing.mdc`.

