When operator says "service A or broker writes to void", verify **each hop** has an asserted sink:

| Hop | Void pattern | Symptom | Holdout / metric |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| UnifiedFilter Lua | `streamKey=fcap:ignored` with no `StreamProducer`/`BrokerProducer` wired | Debit succeeds; no `XADD`/Produce | `TestTryAcquireStreamAdmission_holdoutDeferredNoPublisher`; integration flush |
| StreamProducer | `nil` producers slice or wrong shard index | `filterRejectProducerOverload` or silent drop | `rejectIfStreamProducerOverloaded` tests |
| BrokerProducer | Ring full, `Produce` error swallowed on async path | `ErrRingBufferFull`, post-debit reject metric | `TestBrokerProducer_RingOverflow`, shutdown drain |
| Broker consumer | Consumer group offset stuck; corrupt payload skipped without metric | CH lag, parse error metric flat wrong | `TestFault_BrokerLiveConsumer_CorruptPayload` |
| Processor -> CH | `MockEventStore` in test but prod store misconfigured | Tests green; CH empty | `clickhouse_store_integration_test.go` |
| Local quanta full-skip | Crash before async publish | Spend without event (eventual) | Refill/return Lua + fault drills |

