## Agent-resistant verification (holdouts, fuzz, compiler gates)

Agents optimize for green diffs and tests they can see. This section maps **external anti-slop patterns** to what **this repo actually runs**. Do not claim a gate exists unless a script in `scripts/ci/` or `Makefile` runs it in the cited tier.

Cross-ref: `testing.mdc`, `ci.mdc`, `fault-tests.mdc`, `load-test-bpf.mdc`, `boundaries.mdc` (**Test dishonesty catalog**).

### Proposal vs repo (honest matrix)

| Pattern | Common proposal | In tree today | Agent cannot fake by |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Black-box holdouts | Closed repo / encrypted binary CI; agent never sees asserts | **Partial:** in-repo `*_holdout*` / `TestProof_*`; `merge-integration` + testcontainers Redis/PG/CH; `scripts/fault/run.sh` on `main` | Integration/fault tier (not in `-short`); holdout negative must fail if branch reverted |
| Mutation testing | `go-mutesting`: kill mutants; green after bug injection = fake test | **Not in CI** (no mutation runner in tree) | Holdout negative + `AssertBudgetInvariant`; operator may run mutant manually |
| Compiler gates | `go build -gcflags="-m -m"` fails on heap escape | **Yes (scoped):** `escape_heap_gate.sh` baseline; `hot_path_static_gate.sh`; `lint_go_hotpath_forbid_gate.sh` | Changed hot files: escape line count vs baseline; banned APIs in ingest/rtb |
| Hardware / eBPF perf | `perf stat` / eBPF syscall count per unit test | **Yes (load tier):** BPF probes in load test (`malformed.sh`, `parser_chaos_load.sh`); `bpf/resource.sh` when `PERF_RUNNER_LABEL` set (`ci.mdc`) | Not on every `go test -short`; E2E p99 and outbound connect counters |
| Property / fuzz | `testing/quick` or millions of random inputs | **Yes (scoped):** `Fuzz*` (`FuzzParseTrackJSON`, `FuzzVerifyJWT`, ...); `TestChaos_*`; corpora (`fraudTrackJSONCases2026`, `http1IngressCanonical`); financial `AssertBudgetInvariant` | Random/fuzz input; `differential_count=0` cross-hop; invariant after fault |

**Black-box gap:** holdout tests live **in the same repo** agents edit. They resist slop via **negative cases** and **tier separation** (`pr_fast` vs `make test-integration` vs `make test-fault`), not via hidden asserts. Treat `merge-integration` and `main` resilience as the blind sink for wiring claims.

### 1. Holdouts (in-repo trap tests)

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Naming | `*_holdout`, `*_holdoutPositive`, `TestFoo_withoutBar`, `TestProof_*` |
| Negative required | Must fail if intended branch removed or condition inverted (`TestStreamProducerAdmissionRaceWithoutReserve` pattern) |
| Banned tautology | `require.Equal(t, x, x)`; assert only `err == nil`; mock return wired to assert input |
| Banned scaffold | `scaffold_test:` placeholder; integration file with no `require.*` (`integration_test_slop_gate.sh`) |
| Cite in PR | Touch non-obvious behavior -> name holdout in PR body (`boundaries.mdc` required holdouts table) |

Holdout lie mode: agent adds test that passes whether fix is present (e.g. only checks mock was called). **Falsify:** revert fix locally; holdout must go red.

### 2. Mutation resistance (policy; tooling not shipped)

Mutation runners (`go-mutesting`, etc.) are **not** merge gates in this repo.

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Surrogate | Every non-trivial fix ships an in-repo holdout that would fail if the fix were reverted |
| Fake test signal | Unit test green but deleting production branch still green -> meta-slop; block merge in review |
| Future tier | Optional mutation gate only when it encodes a new matrix; never `exit 0` on failure (`anti-slop.mdc` CI table) |

Do not claim "mutation tested" without pasted mutant-kill output from a runner actually executed.

### 3. Compiler and alloc gates (non-negotiable on hot path)

Comments like `// zero-alloc verified` do not satisfy CI.

| Gate | Command | Fails when |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Heap escape baseline | `bash scripts/ci/static/escape_heap.sh` | New `escapes to heap` in hot files vs `scripts/ci/baselines/escape_hot_path_heap_lines.count` |
| Hot static forbid | `bash scripts/ci/static/hot_path_static.sh`, `lint_go_hotpath_forbid_gate.sh` | `fmt.Sprintf`, `interface{}`, `context.With*` on ingest/rtb hot path |
| Zero-alloc microbench | `make test-alloc-gate` | Hot parse/filter/auction regresses alloc/op |
| Race (shared state) | `bash scripts/ci/race_short.sh` | Data race in `internal/...`, `pkg/...` |

Lie mode: microbench or escape gate cited without pasted command + exit code.

### 4. Fuzz, chaos, and property invariants

Prefer **invariants** over example literals (`input: 5 -> output: 10` only is weak for agents).

| Class | Examples in tree | Invariant or property |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Parser fuzz | `FuzzParseTrackJSON`, `FuzzHTTP1Chunked`, `FuzzParseOpenRTB3FSM` | No panic; budget constants enforced (`parser.mdc`) |
| Security chaos | `TestChaos_ParserSecurity`, `TestChaos_CrossHop_NginxGnet` | `differential_count=0` edge vs gnet |
| Wire corpora | `fraudTrackJSONCases2026`, `http1IngressCanonical` | Reject/accept matrix per case ID |
| Financial | `AssertBudgetInvariant`, stream admission holdouts | `current_spend <= budget_limit`; no debit without sink when deferred |
| License fuzz | `FuzzVerifyJWT` (tiered via `license_verify_tier.sh`) | No panic; crypto smoke timeboxed |

Fuzz lie modes:

| Lie | Reality |
| :--- | :--- |
| `pr_fast` fuzz claim | Fuzz mostly nightly / `license_verify_tier` / smoke scripts |
| Chaos `pct=0` | Test always passes; banned (`fault-tests.mdc`) |
| Fuzz only panics | Must assert reject/match behavior on structured corpora where applicable |

Nightly: `.github/workflows/parser-fuzz-nightly.yaml`; license fuzz via `license_fuzz_nightly_gate.sh` (release tier).

### 5. Tier honesty (what agents run vs what proves wiring)

| Tier | Command | Proves |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `test-fast` / `pr_fast` | `bash scripts/ci/pr_fast.sh`, `make test-fast` | Static gates, unit, holdouts beside code, mocks **scoped** |
| `test-integration` | `make test-integration`, `merge-integration` | testcontainers Redis/PG/CH; real Lua/shard behavior |
| `test-fault` | `make test-fault`, `scripts/fault/run.sh` (main) | Fault injection, budget invariant, resilience proofs |
| `test-alloc-gate` | `make test-alloc-gate` | Hot path alloc budget |
| Load / BPF | `malformed.sh`, `parser_chaos_load.sh`, `bpf/resource.sh` | p99, Redis Lua, tracker outbound connect (`ci.mdc`) |

Claiming production hot-path or sink wiring from **tier 1 only** is a lie (`boundaries.mdc` type E).

### Agent-resistant lie modes (never)

| Lie mode | Example | Falsify |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Tautological assert | `require.Equal(t, got, got)`; table row asserts mock return | Revert production branch; test must fail |
| Mutation survivor | Invert `if` in fix; agent tests still green | Holdout negative; manual mutant review |
| Comment gate | `// escapes heap: no` without `escape_heap_gate.sh` | Run gate on touched hot files |
| Example-only test | Single happy path, no reject/fault row | Corpus row or `*_holdout` negative |
| Black-box fiction | "External CI will catch it" with no tier named | Paste `make test-integration` / fault command |
| BPF on unit test | Claim syscall count on `go test ./...` | Load-test BPF tier only (`load-test-bpf.mdc`) |

## CI and script slop

Agents must not add CI layers that repeat work without new assertions. One gate = one contract; orchestrators compose gates once.

### Banned patterns (reintroduced in 2026 cleanup - do not add back)

| Pattern | Why slop | Canonical shape |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Subset gate duplicating full gate | `check_no_legacy_naming_core.sh` re-scanned `internal/` subset already covered by `naming/legacy_naming.sh` allowlist | Single `naming/legacy_naming.sh` in `pr_fast.sh` |
| Doc gate calling unrelated gate | `naming/antifraud_doc.sh` invoked full legacy naming; `pr_fast` already runs naming before it | `naming/antifraud_doc.sh` = ANTIFRAUD.md vs code only |
| Thin skip gate | `integration_skip_reason_gate.sh` only checked bare `t.Skip()`; subset of `anti_slop_gate.sh` | `anti_slop_gate.sh` + `integration_test_slop_gate.sh` in `pr_fast` |
| Same static scan in two tiers | `tier_a.sh` and `anti_slop_gate.sh` both scanned `_ = json.Unmarshal` / `_ = w.Write` in handlers/outbox | Keep scan in `anti_slop_gate.sh` only |
| Hardcoded script inventory | `naming/scripts_layout.sh` listed ~30 "required" paths that must exist on disk | CI/Makefile ref check + `verify_redis_topology_test.sh` only |
| Fake pass on failure | `license_red_team_garbled.sh` used `exit 0` when garble build failed | Named gate must `exit 1` on failure; optional tier uses env flag + `skip_gate`, not silent pass |
| Always-SKIP gate rows | `license_verify_tier.sh` `release-1` / `release-2` for models not in tree | Omit gate rows; document optional tooling in `DEVELOPMENT.md` if needed |
| Duplicate gate invocation | `admin/web.sh` called `selfserve_nav.sh` twice | One call per gate per orchestrator |
| Matryoshka test orchestrators | `license_red_team.sh` tail-called `license_red_team_extended.sh` while `license_verify_tier` also ran extended | `make license-red-team` = red-team then extended; `license_verify_tier` owns tier matrix |
| Smoke re-running parent gates | `release_qa_smoke.sh` re-ran `license_fuzz_nightly_gate` + extended already in `license_verify_tier` | `release_qa_smoke.sh` = go fuzz smoke + `license_garbled_alloc_gate` only |
| Preflight double admin | `admin_release_preflight_gate.sh` ran `admin/web.sh` then `pr_fast.sh` (which ends with `admin/web`) | `pr_fast` **or** `admin/web` when `ADMIN_RELEASE_SKIP_PR_FAST=1` |
| Smoke before full orchestrator | `cpa_compliance_smoke.sh` called `ui_slop` / `live_routes` then `admin/web.sh` | Call `admin/web.sh` once (sub-gates live inside it) |

### License verify composition (canonical)

| Entry | Runs |
| :--- | :--- |
| `make license-red-team` | `scripts/security/license_red_team.sh` then `scripts/test/license/red_team_extended.sh` |
| `make license-verify` | `scripts/ci/license/verify_tier.sh` (baseline, crypto, entangle, release-4..6 optional, alloc) |
| `release_qa_smoke.sh` | Fuzz targets + `license_garbled_alloc_gate` only; not fuzz_nightly or extended |

Do not add a new `*_gate.sh` whose body is only `bash` lines to other gates unless it encodes a new env matrix or fail-closed contract. Prefer extending the leaf gate or the single orchestrator (`pr_fast.sh`, `license/verify_tier.sh`, `admin/web.sh`).

## Documentation lie modes (never)

Applies to `README.md`, `docs/`, `deploy/vendor/`, admin user-visible copy, Grafana panel text. Engineering tone only: paths, HTTP codes, SLA from `core.mdc`, license facts from `sku.yaml`.

| Lie | What code actually does | Write instead |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Microbench as prod SLA | `BenchmarkFilterFraudBoost` ~90 ns/op is isolated `FilterEngine.Check`; prod is full chain + Redis Lua | Name bench; E2E p99 from load test / Prometheus |
| "Reads boost in-memory under 90 ns" beside Redis | Boost snapshot is Go `atomic.Value` map; ML writer uses Redis in background | "Snapshot lookup in Go; Redis sync async" |
| "Eliminated `SISMEMBER` / `HEXISTS` / INCR" | `FraudBlacklistFilter` still `SISMEMBER`; placement cache misses `HEXISTS`; RPD uses Redis `INCR` | "Cached with Redis on miss" or implement cache first |
| "Local atomic ingress RPD" | `EntitlementsFilter` / `lua_precheck` Redis `INCR` | State Redis INCR or implement local counter |
| `silent_reject_enabled` "wired" | Only PG migration + admin PATCH; hot path ignored flag | `fraudTrackOutcome` reads registry; holdout tests; decoy 202/302 vs 403 |
| ML `ghost` / `silent_reject` action | Per-IP decoy or auto-enable campaign | Outbox adds IP to `blacklist:fraud`; does not `UPDATE silent_reject_enabled`; legacy action alias `ghost` only on enqueue |
| IVT tier ML "enforcement" | Doc implies all tiers get boost/blacklist | `FraudTierIVT` with flag off must blacklist or document no-op; suspect=boost, block=blacklist |
| L2 shadow billing omitted | "Shadow accepted, logged to CH" | State whether `UnifiedFilter` Lua ran; fraud signals before Lua skip debit when short-circuited |
| Fraud stream parity | "All fraud rejects in CH" | Silent accept enqueues fraud stream; hard 403 must too if funnels count blocks |
| `silent_reject_event` unset | Silent reject returns 202 but analytics empty | Set event flag on silent accept; CH column `silent_reject_event`; not legacy `ghost_event` in new code |
| XDP stops residential fraud | XDP drops listed L3/L4; rotating proxies evade host maps | "L4 flood + known IPs"; optional `ebpf_xdp_edge` |
| XDP token bucket "starvation bug" | Legacy `last_ns=now` on every pass is stricter than config, not 100% drop above rate | Cite `TestTokenBucket_subintervalCredit_holdout`; fixed in `token_bucket_consume_existing` |
| XDP PERCPU "race" on lookup+update | PERCPU shards are per-CPU; in-place mutate is safe; issue was redundant `update_elem` | `edge.mdc` PERCPU table |
| XDP ICMP "tracker scoped" | IPv4 ICMP was global drop; PMTUD Type 3 Code 4 now `XDP_PASS` | `TestXDP_dropNonTCPOnTrackerPort/icmp_pmtud_pass` |
| XDP fingerprint MSS | `read_tcp_mss` must TLV-walk options (NOP before MSS) | `TCPOPT_NOP` in `TestEdgeFilterRateLimitPerCPUHash_holdout` |
| XDP syn-cookie "full TCP" | SYN-ACK is doff=5 by design; not a parser bug | `TestFault_XDPSynCookieWithTCPOptions` |
| XDP tail-call "wired" | Miss must emit violation+stat; silent return banned | `syn_cookie_tail_call` + `goto out` in `edge.mdc` |
| XDP math from prog.Test only | `prog.Test` needs CAP_BPF; bucket proof is Go sim | `xdp-bpf.mdc` **Verification tiers** |
| JA3/TCP MSS as client signals | Tracker reads edge headers; CDN terminates TCP | CDN disclaimer; `edge.mdc` disable flags |
| "Guarantee", "never" (ML on hot path) | OK if qualified: ML in sidecar only | "Batch only"; cite `cmd/fraud-scorer` |
| Mixed ns / us / ms in one claim | Different layers have different budgets | Table per layer: edge, local filter, Redis Lua, handler E2E |
| Detached filter goroutine | `FilterEngine.Check` is synchronous on `PinnedWorkerPool` Tier B (`trackwire.go`); epoll Tier A only enqueues | `hot-path.mdc` **Tracker thread model**; `cmd/tracker/doc.go` |
| Pinned workers return to epoll | Only gnet epoll returns after `SubmitOffload`; workers run full path incl. sync `EVALSHA` | Tier A vs Tier B table in `hot-path.mdc` |
| `unsafe.String` over gnet frame through filter | Frame discarded before filter; pin/arena lifetime on Tier B worker | `tradeoffs.mdc` offload buffers; `cloneAsyncWriteBytes` before release |
| Magic numbers in `doc.go` | Informal; use Defaults and limits / Env defaults with units | `comments.mdc` **Forbidden in doc.go** |
| `doc.go` ports or subcommands stale | Must match `main.go` / `wire.go` / `config` defaults | `comments.mdc` **cmd doc.go sync** |

Open implementation gaps: `deploy/vendor/ANTIFRAUD.md` (semantic slugs in prose, not ticket IDs). Do not close gaps in docs alone.

CI: `bash scripts/ci/naming/antifraud_doc.sh` (in `pr_fast.sh`; stale hot-path text, false eliminated claims, legacy naming in vendor docs). Marketing prose: `naming.mdc`.

Script: `bash scripts/ci/static/anti_slop.sh` (included in `pr_fast.sh`).

Scope: `internal/controlplane`, `internal/ingestion`, `internal/payment`, `pkg/`.

| Pattern | Why banned |
| :--- | :--- |
| Bare `t.Skip()` | Hides missing coverage |
| `t.Skip("skipping integration test")` without `integration:` prefix | Gate cannot distinguish real skip |
| `testing.Short()` skip without `integration:` in reason | Same |
| `testing.Testing()` in non-test `.go` | Test hook in production code |
| `os.Getenv("CI")` branch in prod | Environment-specific behavior |
| `_ = json.Unmarshal` / `_ = w.Write` in `*_handlers.go`, `outbox_*.go` | Silent handler failures |
| `nolint:errcheck` without ticket | Permanent error swallow |
| `BenchmarkUnifiedFilter_Check` (unqualified) | Must be `_mock` - uses mock Redis |
| `httptest.NewServer` in package that also uses testcontainers for DB | Fake infra when real PG/Redis required |

## Integration test slop

Script: `bash scripts/ci/static/integration_test_slop.sh`.

Every `*_integration_test.go` must:

1. Guard with `testing.Short()` and skip reason containing `integration:`.
2. Call a real infra helper (`testutil.SetupPostgres`, `SetupRedis`, `setupTestDB`, etc.).
3. Contain behavioral assertions (`require.*` / `assert.*`).
4. Never use `testify/mock`, `gomock`, or bare `t.Skip()`.
5. Never leave scaffold placeholders (`scaffold_test: add a held-out negative assertion` only).

## Hot-path static slop

Scripts: `hot_path_static_gate.sh`, `lint_go_hotpath_forbid_gate.sh`, `escape_heap_gate.sh`.

Files: `handler.go`, `handler_http*.go`, `filter*.go`, `filters.go`, `internal/rtb/*.go`.

Banned in hot request path:

- `fmt.Sprintf`, `interface{}` boxing, `context.WithValue`
- `context.WithTimeout` / `context.WithCancel` in request-path sources and `internal/domain` (except allowlisted cold broker/store files)

New heap escapes above baseline or in changed hot files fail `escape_heap_gate.sh`. After hot-path edits run `make test-alloc-gate`.

## Cold-path static slop

Scripts: `cold_path_static_gate.sh`, `cold_path_json_gate.sh`.

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Redis commands | No `KEYS`, `FLUSHALL`, `FLUSHDB` in production Go |
| N+1 queries | No new O(N) DB-in-loop patterns in changed controlplane/payment/ledger files |
| Body limits | `pkg/coldpath.DefaultMaxBody=64KiB`; handlers use `ReadLimitedBody` / `DecodeRequestOrBadRequest` - not raw `io.ReadAll` |

Run: `bash scripts/ci/static/cold_path_static.sh`; `go test ./pkg/coldpath/ -run TestReadLimitedBody`.

