## Admin UI slop

Scripts: `check_ui_slop.sh`, `report_live_routes_gate.sh` (when `web/` exists).

**Status:** `web/` active. Before new admin UI: explicit operator spec + `ui.mdc` contract (Tailwind + shadcn/ui).

Forbidden when `web/src/**` exists:

- `(skeleton)` in user-visible copy
- "not fully available yet" / "Skeleton shows expected"
- Empty table blaming user to "connect API"
- `live: true` on route without real `/api/v1` backend
- Fetch then always empty table; `catch` -> empty with no error UI
- "Saved" toast before 2xx; form fields not in Go DTO
- Hardcoded demo KPIs; echoing secrets/tokens after save

Required when shipping admin UI: read handler DTO first; `StubBanner` for 501; `ErrorBlock` on errors; no silent `catch` -> empty table; `apiConfirmed` before success toast; `npm run typecheck`; `bash scripts/ci/admin/web.sh`; paste verification commands in PR.

Forbidden in admin copy and embed snippets (when `web/` exists):

- Report catalog keys/titles `ghost-impression-funnel`, column headers "Ghost" when API field is `silent_reject_*` (canonical route `silent-reject-impression-funnel`; legacy URL alias ok one release)
- Product-prefixed static filenames (`ad-event-processor-track.js`); use neutral `track.js` and export `trackEvent` when static tree returns
- User-visible "fixed" for antifraud flags when only admin toggle or migration landed

## Code slop patterns (no dedicated gate - still reject)

- Provider/Factory/Strategy interfaces with one implementation (`cold-path.mdc`).
- Repository interface over sqlc when `db.Queries` suffices.
- `map[string]any` JSON builders on cold path.
- Parallel Entity/Model/View/DTO for same table.
- `defer` in hot-path loops; closures capturing per-request state on `/track`.
- Dynamic Prometheus label values built per request in filter loops.
- Importing `internal/fraud` scoring into tracker ingest.
- Postgres/ClickHouse/outbox side effects inside `processTrack()` or filter `Check`.
- Hand-editing `*.pb.go`, `*.sql.go`, bpf2go output.
- Docs-only commits without code in the same changeset (`core.mdc`).
- Cold-path ML enforcement that mutates operator campaign config (`silent_reject_enabled`) instead of per-IP Redis/CH effects.
- Empty `garble_policy.go` or missing `//garble:ignore` while `TestGarblePolicy_ingestionPackageIgnored` expects it.
- God package or god `controlplane` growth: new domain logic in composition root or bridge instead of `internal/<domain>/` (`modular-monolith.mdc`).
- New `*_aliases.go` or filename-prefix `domains.go` classification (`modular-monolith.mdc` **Migration cruft ban**).
- Bridge file with SQL, validation, or report math — wiring and DTO map only (`modular-monolith.mdc`).
- `Host` / `Effects` port expanded past 12 methods without splitting the port first.
- New `internal/<domain>/` stub (types/host only, or missing `doc.go`) or `internal/common` util package — minimum viable extraction (`modular-monolith.mdc`).
- Premature package split while parent is still under god ceilings and no named extraction task.

## Fault and chaos proof slop

- `fault_proof proof=open` without follow-up test or explicit PR waiver.
- Chaos tests that pass only because chaos pct is 0.
- Parser security change without `TestChaos_CrossHop_NginxGnet` `differential_count=0`.
- New hot-path write path without fault proof (`fault-tests.mdc`).

## Agent local environment (operator-owned)

The operator machine is not a CI runner. Shared dev hosts OOM when agents loop `go build`, `go test`, or full-repo typecheck. **Default: read code, `read_lints`, `grep`, `gofmt -e` on touched files only.** Do not compile or test to "double-check" or "be safe" unless the operator asked in the current turn or a named gate is required for the claim (see **When compile/test is allowed**).

### Compile and test ritual ban (never)

| Pattern | Why banned |
| :--- | :--- |
| `go build ./...`, `go test ./...`, `go test -c ./...` | Full module graph; downloads deps; OOM risk |
| `go build` / `go test -c` on whole packages after a green run in the same turn | Ritual re-verify; no new signal |
| Chaining builds (`build` then `test -c` then `vet` on same scope) without operator ask | Multiplies RAM/CPU for the same package |
| `npm run typecheck` / `npx tsc` on full `web/` without operator ask or UI claim | Heavy; use `read_lints` on edited TSX first |
| "Verify syntax" via compile when `read_lints` + `gofmt -e` + `go list -e` on touched package suffice | Compile is not the default syntax check |
| Claiming green build/tests without pasted command + exit code | `quality.mdc` verification honesty |

### Forbidden without explicit operator ask

| Action | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| `go build ./...`, `go test ./...`, `go test -c ./...` | Full-repo compile/test; OOM on shared machines |
| `go build -o /dev/null ./internal/...` or `./cmd/...` (multi-package) | Same; scope wider than one edited package |
| `go test -c -o /dev/null ./internal/<pkg>/` when operator did not ask to verify that package | Test compile still links deps; not a default step |
| `npm run typecheck`, `bash scripts/ci/admin/web.sh` (full web gate) | Full admin web tier |
| `bash scripts/dev/stack/stack.sh` (any subcommand except `down` when operator asks to stop) | Full compose: tracker, processor, control, PG, Redis, ClickHouse, nginx, broker |
| `docker compose up` / `docker compose start` under `deploy/compose/` | Same stack; duplicates `stack.sh` |
| `bash scripts/ci/prepare_test.sh` | Brings up compose and waits for ClickHouse |
| `make test-integration`, `make test-fault`, `scripts/fault/run.sh`, `compose_fault_drill.sh` | testcontainers + long-running fault matrix |
| `make test-fast`, full `bash scripts/ci/pr_fast.sh`, `go test ./internal/... ./pkg/...` | Heavy RAM/CPU; can OOM the IDE |
| Repeated `escape_heap_gate.sh` / `go build -gcflags=-m` on unchanged hot files | Large logs; marginal value per rerun |
| Load test / BPF gates (`malformed.sh`, `parser_chaos_load.sh`, `bpf/resource.sh`) | Needs running stack and sustained traffic |

### When compile/test is allowed

Only if **one** of these is true in the current turn:

| Trigger | Allowed scope |
| :--- | :--- |
| Operator explicitly asks ("run tests", "build", "verify compile", "pr_fast") | Exactly what they asked; paste command + exit code |
| Claiming a specific gate passed (`test-alloc-gate`, `pr_fast`, named `-run`) | That gate only; once per claim |
| Hot-path binary wiring change and operator asked for tracker proof | `go build -o /dev/null ./cmd/tracker/` once |
| Scoped test operator named | `go test ./<pkg>/ -short -run TestFoo -count=1` once |

If none apply: state **not run** and what lightweight check you used (`read_lints`, `grep`, `gofmt -e`, `go list -e ./path/...`).

### Allowed default verification (no compile)

| Scope | Example |
| :--- | :--- |
| IDE / static diagnostics | `read_lints` on edited paths |
| Obvious syntax / import drift | `grep`, `gofmt -e` on touched `.go` files |
| Package graph error without linking | `go list -e ./internal/controlplane/...` (single subtree; not `./...`) |
| One holdout, operator asked or behavior claim | `go test ./internal/ingestion/ -short -run TestFoo_holdout -count=1` |
| Single static gate on touched files | `bash scripts/ci/static/escape_heap.sh` once after hot-path edit |
| Stop stack when operator complains or asks | `bash scripts/dev/stack/stack.sh down` |

When verification needs integration tier or full compile, **name the command** and ask the operator to run it locally; do not auto-start compose or loop builds.

## Agent checklist before "done"

| Step | Command / action |
| :--- | :--- |
| 1 | New symbols: `read_lints` + `grep`/`gofmt -e` on touched files; `go build`/`go test` only when operator asked or step 3 names a gate |
| 2 | Hot path does not import cold fraud scoring |
| 3 | Paste command + package path for verification runs actually executed |
| 4 | Explain why scripts/tests changed |
| 5 | Add a test that fails without the change when behavior is non-obvious |
| 6 | Doc claims match code or cite `ANTIFRAUD.md` slug; run `naming/antifraud_doc.sh` when touching vendor antifraud docs |
| 7 | Run `pr_fast` or scoped `go test` only when operator asked; never full-repo `-short` or compose prep |
| 8 | Antifraud: verify silent reject path (flag, decoy HTTP, stream/CH flag, ML action) in code before closing backlog item |
| 9 | New CI script: no duplicate gate in parent + child; no `exit 0` on failed check; no hardcoded "must exist" script lists |
| 10 | Doc-only operator ask: no code/CI/Docker diff in same turn |
| 11 | Admin UI: operator spec + `ui.mdc` contract before `web/src/**` |
| 12 | Operator stop signal: revert slice, do not layer fixes |
| 13 | Hot path claim: name tier (`test-fast` / `test-integration` / `test-fault` / `test-alloc-gate`) actually run |
| 14 | Hot path: no "wired" from `mockRedisClient`, `mockBrokerClient`, or `MockEventStore` alone |
| 15 | Non-obvious fix: add `*_holdout` negative that fails if branch reverted (`testing.mdc`) |
| 16 | No tautology / mutation-survivor tests; name verification **tier** (`Agent-resistant verification`) |
| 17 | No god package: new admin logic in domain package; bridge wiring only; port <=12 methods (`modular-monolith.mdc`) |
| 18 | No micro-package: new domain dir only with handlers/store + wire + `doc.go` in same PR; no `internal/common` (`modular-monolith.mdc`) |
| 19 | Every production package has detailed `doc.go` (role, verify commands); edit in the same PR when adding a package (`comments.mdc`, `modular-monolith.mdc`) |

